MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Blak and Blu fits the expressive blues-rock guitar I have been drawn to through Hendrix and Clapton, making it my strongest next choice.",
    "In My Soul connects with the soulful blues appeal of Memphis and Old Sock; guitar playing together with soulful vocals feels especially right today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Endless River and Days Of Future Passed miss my current interest in blues guitar and vocals; atmospheric or orchestral rock does not offer the same appeal.",
    "The Alligator collection and I Am The Blues relate to my interests, but a broad compilation or a more traditional blues sound is less compelling than a contemporary artist album today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "An association with classic rock seems to count too much when the actual listening experience can be far from the soulful blues I want.",
    "Being blues-related alone does not make every album equally appealing; compilations, traditional blues, and contemporary blues-rock serve different moods for me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of expressive guitar and soulful singing matters more to me right now than a broad connection to rock.",
    "I rarely choose many albums at once: Blak and Blu and In My Soul are enough for this visit, while other relevant albums can wait."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in blues and guitar-led music, but sometimes stretched that interest beyond the soulful, contemporary sound I want today."
}
